{"returncode": 0, "stdout": "\n==========================================================================\n  Submit and Run A Batch Job in Express Queue on Hopper GPU Cluster\n==========================================================================\n\n\u001b[1;31m  --- Sample job submission script [job1.txt] in GREEN starts from the below line -->> \u001b[0m\n\u001b[1;32m#!/bin/bash \u001b[0m\n\u001b[1;32m#PBS -P Project-Name \u001b[0m\n\u001b[1;32m#PBS -q autox \u001b[0m\n\u001b[1;32m#PBS -j oe \u001b[0m\n\u001b[1;32m#PBS -k oed \u001b[0m\n\u001b[1;32m#PBS -N pytorch_job \u001b[0m\n\u001b[1;32m#PBS -l walltime=24:00:00 \u001b[0m\n\u001b[1;32m#PBS -l select=1:ngpus=1 \u001b[0m\n\u001b[1;32m# \u001b[0m\n\u001b[1;33m##----- CPU/Mem will be allocated at 12/225gb per GPU. -----\u001b[0m\n\u001b[1;33m##----- Please Replace the Project-Name with your actual project, e.g. CFP04-SF-XXX ---\u001b[0m\n\u001b[1;33m##----- sample config for ngpus of 2, 4, 8, 16 via either line below ---- \u001b[0m\n\u001b[1;33m###PBS -l select=1:ngpus=2 \u001b[0m\n\u001b[1;33m###PBS -l select=1:ngpus=4 \u001b[0m\n\u001b[1;33m###PBS -l select=1:ngpus=8 \u001b[0m\n\u001b[1;33m###PBS -l select=2:ngpus=8 \u001b[0m\n\n\u001b[1;32mcd $PBS_O_WORKDIR; \u001b[0m\n\n\u001b[1;32mimage=\"/app1/common/singularity-img/hopper/cuda/cuda_12.1.0-cudnn8-devel-u20.04.sif\" \u001b[0m\n\u001b[1;32mmodule load singularity \u001b[0m\n\n\u001b[1;32msingularity exec $image bash << EOF > stdout.$PBS_JOBID 2> stderr.$PBS_JOBID \u001b[0m\n\u001b[1;32msource /scratch/ccekwk/virtualenvs/axolotl/bin/activate  \u001b[0m\n\n\u001b[1;32mpython cifar10_resnet.py \u001b[0m\n\n\u001b[1;31m##************************************************************************** \u001b[0m\n\u001b[1;31m##   WARNING and IMPORTANT NOTICE                                          * \u001b[0m\n\u001b[1;31m##************************************************************************** \u001b[0m\n\u001b[1;31m##   DON'T SET  [CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES]  in your Python Program!            * \u001b[0m\n\u001b[1;31m##   PBS Job Scheduler will set GPU devices for the job automatically.     * \u001b[0m\n\u001b[1;31m##************************************************************************** \u001b[0m\n\n\u001b[1;32m# you can put more commands here \u001b[0m\n\u001b[1;32m# echo \"Hello World\" \u001b[0m\n\u001b[1;32mEOF \u001b[0m\n\u001b[1;31m  <<--- End at the above line with EOF ----- \u001b[0m\n\n Make necessary changes to the above script file [job1.txt], then \n you can submit the job, check job status, and check cluster loading status by:\n Enter this command to find out the 'Project-Name' for your account: \u001b[1;31m hpc project \u001b[0m\n\n  # \u001b[1;32mqsub  job1.txt     ##--- To submit a batch job via script <job1.txt> \u001b[0m\n  # \u001b[1;32mqstat -awn1        ##--- To list batch jobs with wide format and show exec nodes \u001b[0m\n  # \u001b[1;32mqstat -fx job_id   ##--- To list details of a batch job <job_id> \u001b[0m\n  # \u001b[1;32mqgpu_smi  job_id   ##--- To check GPU and CPU load of a running job  \u001b[0m\n  # \u001b[1;32mgstat              ##--- To check overall loading status of hopper cluster and queue  \u001b[0m\n\n\n\u001b[1;31m More examples and instructions are available at this URL: \u001b[0m\n\n https://nusit.nus.edu.sg/hpc/ --> Hopper Onboarding.\n\n", "stderr": ""}
